@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1050 = private unnamed_addr constant [1067 x i8] c"## Deprecation\0A\0AThis rule was deprecated as the `lxml` library has been modified to address\0Aknown vulnerabilities and unsafe defaults. As such, the `defusedxml`\0Alibrary is no longer necessary, `defusedxml` has [deprecated] its `lxml`\0Amodule.\0A\0A## What it does\0AChecks for uses of insecure XML parsers.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AMany XML parsers are vulnerable to XML attacks (such as entity expansion),\0Awhich cause excessive memory and CPU usage by exploiting recursion. An\0Aattacker could use such methods to access unauthorized resources.\0A\0AIn [preview], this rule will also flag references to insecure XML parsers.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom lxml import etree\0A\0Acontent = etree.parse(\22untrusted.xml\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PyPI: `lxml`](https://pypi.org/project/lxml/)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-400](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-776](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/776.html)\0A\0A[preview]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/\0A[deprecated]: https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/0.8.0rc2/#defusedxml-lxml\0A", align 1
