@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1242 = private unnamed_addr constant [21 x i8] c"pandas-use-of-dot-iat", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1243 = private unnamed_addr constant [1077 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `.iat` on Pandas objects.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `.iat` method selects a single value from a `DataFrame` or Series based\0Aon an ordinal index, and is slightly faster than using `.iloc`. However,\0A`.iloc` is more idiomatic and versatile, as it can be used to select\0Amultiple values at once.\0A\0AIf performance is an important consideration, convert the object to a NumPy\0Aarray, which will provide a much greater performance boost than using `.iat`\0Aover `.iloc`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Astudents_df = pd.read_csv(\22students.csv\22)\0Astudents_df.iat[0]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Astudents_df = pd.read_csv(\22students.csv\22)\0Astudents_df.iloc[0]\0A```\0A\0AOr, using NumPy:\0A```python\0Aimport numpy as np\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Astudents_df = pd.read_csv(\22students.csv\22)\0Astudents_df.to_numpy()[0]\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Pandas documentation: `iloc`](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.iloc.html)\0A- [Pandas documentation: `iat`](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.iat.html)\0A", align 1
