@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1246 = private unnamed_addr constant [34 x i8] c"mixed-case-variable-in-class-scope", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1247 = private unnamed_addr constant [909 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for class variable names that follow the `mixedCase` convention.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends that variable names should be lower case and separated\0Aby underscores (also known as `snake_case`).\0A\0A> Function names should be lowercase, with words separated by underscores\0A> as necessary to improve readability.\0A>\0A> Variable names follow the same convention as function names.\0A>\0A> mixedCase is allowed only in contexts where that\E2\80\99s already the\0A> prevailing style (e.g. threading.py), to retain backwards compatibility.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass MyClass:\0A    myVariable = \22hello\22\0A    another_variable = \22world\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass MyClass:\0A    my_variable = \22hello\22\0A    another_variable = \22world\22\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#function-and-method-arguments\0A", align 1
